course: dictionary
lesson: 13018
title: Eyeglasses and everyday words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Eyeglasses is a noun. It names two lenses set in a frame that you wear in front of your eyes to help you see better. It is a plural word, so it names a pair, like trousers or scissors.
explain: The words around it give you clues. «She put on her eyeglasses to read the small print.» Reading small print is hard without help, so eyeglasses must be something that helps you see clearly.
explain: In Britain most people say glasses, but in American books and films you may hear eyeglasses. Check by swapping in glasses: if the sentence still makes sense, the meaning is the same.
fact: Eyeglasses means glasses: two lenses in a frame worn in front of the eyes.
fact: Eyeglasses is a plural noun, so it names a pair, as in «a pair of eyeglasses».
fact: «Wear eyeglasses» means put them on your face to help you see better.
fact: An optician tests your eyes to see whether you need eyeglasses.
fact: Lenses in eyeglasses bend light so that it focuses clearly on the eye, which helps people see better.
exercise: «My grandad wears eyeglasses to read the newspaper.» What are eyeglasses? | A pair of gloves for cold weather | A tool for cutting paper | A kind of hat for the sun | *Glasses with two lenses in a frame, worn in front of the eyes
exercise: In Britain people usually say a different word for eyeglasses. Which word do they say? | kettles | *glasses | torches | mittens
exercise: «The optician tested her eyes, then gave her a pair of eyeglasses.» Who tests your eyes before you get eyeglasses? | *An optician | A dentist | A bus driver | A baker
test: «Lenses bend light so that it focuses clearly.» What do the lenses in eyeglasses do? | Make the frame stronger | Turn the room dark | *Bend light so you can see clearly | Keep your ears warm
test: Which phrase shows you put eyeglasses on your face? | Bake eyeglasses | *Wear eyeglasses | Sing eyeglasses | Eat eyeglasses
exam: «Ella's eyeglasses were broken, so she could not read the board.» What does eyeglasses mean? | *Glasses to help you see | Pens for writing | Something to drink | A type of sport
